// AnalysisRuntimeArtifactWorkTeaching keeps task planning separate from both
// code-path selection and the number of rows expected in an answer.
const AnalysisRuntimeArtifactWorkTeaching = "Optional runtime_artifact_work_profile describes the CURRENT user's policy for inspecting a collection of captures: mode=representative with a positive integer per_specification_limit for an explicitly stated per-group budget, or mode=exhaustive with no budget for an explicit all-members check. Copy a short contiguous source_quote from that request. Interpret the number semantically in any language (for example 两份 / two / 2 all yield 2); the quote need not contain an ASCII numeral. Omit the profile when no explicit collection-work policy or representative budget is given; never invent a budget. This is not enumeration_boundary (answer cardinality), runtime_selection_profile (code implementation selection), statistical representativeness, or measured sample count. Keep target threads/processes in runtime_targets and windows in runtime_artifact_scope_profile. The work declaration grants no source, query-result, execution, completion, or causal authority; later explicit tools must choose an ordinary query view and an authorized root. Requested budgets above tool capacity remain requested, not silently capped."
